# AI Tool Governance

<!-- merged from: atlas/26-ai-tool-governance -->

- Every agentic loop must have a **hard iteration cap**. Never use an unbounded loop.
- Tools may only be called from a fixed, approved registry. No dynamic tool dispatch.
- Tool results must be validated and sanitised before further processing or re-submission to an LLM.
- All tool calls are recorded in the audit trail: `tool_name`, `tool_input`, `tool_result`.
- **HITL is mandatory** at design-control approval, risk acceptance, DMR finalise, release gate, and any Class C change.
- AI drafts and proposes — a human approves. No silent writes to regulated records.
- Enforce cost guardrails per run; halt on budget breach and log the current spend vs budget.
